  "details": "The configuration of both World Lists and Group Membership allows us to determine who can view it.\n\nThe options include: No one, Only Friends, and Everyone.\n\nThese access levels function identically for both World Lists and Group Membership.\n\nHowever, they are labeled differently in their respective menus:\n\nFor lists, the labels are **Private**, **Friends**, and **Public**.\n\nFor membership, the labels are **Visible**, **Friends Only**, and **Hidden**.\n\nIn that particular order!\n\nTo improve consistency, it would be beneficial to standardize the access levels, their names, and tooltips across both features.\n\nAs more features with configurable privacy settings are likely to be introduced in the future, maintaining a uniform naming convention will prevent confusion and enhance user experience.\n\nThis is also related to\n\n- https://feedback.vrchat.com/localization/p/split-22429-public\n\n- https://feedback.vrchat.com/localization/p/split-22507-friends",
